description:
The contract between catalog/islamic-service-landscape.json and generator/generate.py. Catalog v1 carried three fields per service domain {name, functionalPattern, assetType}, which is why all 48 generated services were byte-identical scaffolds: the generator had nothing per-domain to work from. v2 adds the per-domain data from which ONE template derives a real OpenAPI schema, a Flyway migration, a repository, a rules component and an AsyncAPI document. The 49th domain costs one entry in this file and nothing else.

THREE THINGS THIS SCHEMA EXISTS TO PREVENT:
  1. a silent scaffold — generate.py validates against this schema and REFUSES to stamp a malformed entry rather than falling back to additionalProperties:true;
  2. a float in a money path — `money` is int64 MINOR units and `ratio` is an exact integer pair, and neither has a decimal form anywhere in this schema;
  3. a manufactured compliance claim — every `shariah` block is reviewed:false and every Shariah-bearing rule carries its citation, or it is reported as a gap.

NOT A SHARIAH ARTEFACT. Nothing described by this schema has been reviewed by a Shariah supervisory board. Standards are cited by body and number; no clause was read from a primary text. See `shariahReview` at the root.
